 "note": "L6 RELAY WORKS. A's three relay nodes stand in a column in front of H, each with a fixed lane toward B: R1 (the laser) the short top lane to L1, R2 (the forge) the short middle lane to F1, R3 (the monster hub) the long bottom lane R3 - M1 - M2 (two long decks; M2, the lane's end, is 2 bridges from the hub, within the monster's 3). All three are retracts whose decks the lesson never fires or routes over: R1 - R2 and R2 - R3 join A's own relays, R3 - F1 is a diagonal B's scripted lines never take (each lane is their short way). Names: H, R1 (laser), R2 (forge), R3 (monster hub), L1, F1, M1, M2 (the monster lane's end), BH.",
